  "notes": "A gentle, comforting action of rubbing or stroking a body part. Commonly used when soothing someone who is in pain, feeling sick, or crying. The motion is light and repetitive, distinct from a firm massage.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {背中|せなか}をさする: to rub someone's back\n- お{腹|なか}をさする: to rub one's tummy\n- {肩|かた}をさする: to rub one's shoulders\n- {膝|ひざ}をさする: to rub one's knees\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {撫|な}でる: to stroke, to pet (lighter touch, often for hair or animals)\n- {揉|も}む: to knead, to massage (firmer pressure)\n- こする: to rub (more vigorous, can imply friction or scrubbing)",
